{"id":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Agents","desc":"Who can be dispatched, one node per agent. THE EXACT LAUNCH COMMAND is the `command` PROPERTY — a launcher reads it and runs it verbatim; a missing node, or a node without `command`, REFUSES the spawn loudly; nobody falls back to a machine default (the Fable burn, 2026-08-13, is why this file exists). `role` says what the agent is for — `prop:role=reviewer` lists the review bench, `prop:role=author` who can hold a lane. The note keeps the story and the quirks; the properties keep the facts. Spawn shape: `kolu create --repo <repo> --worktree <branch> --json -- <command>`. When kolu grows a structured launch spec, these properties migrate into it.","changed":"2026-08-15T18:43:29-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"claude-opus — the author agent","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Opus, YOLO mode. The default author for dispatched lanes. Verify with the banner: it must say Opus, not the machine default.","changed":"2026-08-15T18:43:29-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"grok — reviewer","desc":"Grok CLI in always-approve mode. Reviews in a split terminal of the author's worktree; posts one review comment via gh; never edits, pushes, or merges.","changed":"2026-08-15T18:43:31-04:00","custom":{"command":"grok --always-approve","role":"reviewer"}}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2","title":"opencode — reviewer","desc":"opencode TUI on its configured model (kimi-k3 via Juspay at last sighting — the config is opencode's own, not spelled here). Same reviewer contract as grok. Known quirk: has mislabeled itself \"codex\" in a posted review once; brief it to title reviews with its tool name.","changed":"2026-08-15T18:43:31-04:00","custom":{"command":"opencode","role":"reviewer"}}
